# The erhai device package set's release counter.  One line, <epoch-free
# upstream version>, and the last component is bumped by hand for each release
# that is meant to be installed over the previous one.
#
# It is the only thing in the .deb version that dpkg's ordering ever reaches:
# everything after it identifies the build, and two builds of the same release
# never differ in it.  So a release that is not bumped will not install over
# its predecessor, and apt is right to say so.
